# Paths a person reviews, whoever opened the pull request.
#
# The set is the wire contract and the suite that is its authority. Everything
# here is either the schema itself, generated from it, or the thing that decides
# whether an implementation speaks it -- and version skew makes all of it
# irreversible: a tenant's sidecar is upgraded on the tenant's schedule or never
# (docs/why/version-skew.md).
#
# !! THE HANDLE BELOW IS A PLACEHOLDER AND MUST BE REPLACED. !!
# GitHub silently ignores a CODEOWNERS line naming an account that cannot be
# found -- no error, no warning, and the rule simply does not apply. A file in
# this state looks exactly like protection and is none, which is why
# rebuild-plugboard task 1.9 is not complete until a real owner is substituted
# and a bot-authored pull request touching contract/ is observed to be blocked.

/contract/        @OWNER-HANDLE-REPLACE-ME
/conformance/     @OWNER-HANDLE-REPLACE-ME

